+  # match-on-chip USB sensors (ThinkPad X13 Gen 2i: 06cb:00f9) and is only added when one is on the bus now, so every other laptop
+  # keeps Google's setup. Its service declares IFingerprint/default too: init then rejects crosfp's definition, which it parses
+  # later from the APEX ("Interface ... redefined"), so only one HAL can own the interface. FINGERPRINT=0 in gbos.cfg turns it off.
